      "text": "The question states that Hal changes the batteries every 5 months. Since he just changed them in May (the 5th month), the **25th** change will occur in the **200**-month period.\n\nTo break it down:\n\n* The **1st and 5th months** were changed in May.\n* For a 5-month cycle, the next change (10th month) would be in the **6th and 11th months**.\n* Continuing this pattern:\n\t+ 5 * 4 (remainder 1) = 21st month\n\nThe **21st month** falls in **November**.\n\nNow, we need to find the month before the 25th change:\n\n* Subtracting the first change (May) from November returns us to **May**.\n* Moving forward from May (which is the 6th month of November),\n* We encounter the **25th month**, which falls in **December**.\n\nTherefore, the batteries will be changed for the **25th time** in the **December** month.",
