changed in step #10 (used for calculating after 5 units).\n14. When the 14th set is changed:\n    - His month + 5 × 13 months, this takes them into Winter again, which can be July.\n15. When the 15th set is changed:\n    - His month + 5 × 14 months, takes us to Winter once again, which was mentioned in step #12.\n16. When the 16th set is changed:\n    - His month + 5 × 15 months, takes them into Summer, which was mentioned in step #6.\n17. When the 17th set is changed:\n    - His month + 5 × 16 months, takes them into Summer again, which was mentioned in step #3.\n18. When the 18th set is changed:\n    - His month + 5 × 17 months, keeps the same month (though seasonal issues are more seasonally predictable).\n19. When the 19th set is changed:\n    - His month + 5 × 18 months, keeps the same month (though seasonal issues are more seasonally predictable).\n20. When the 20th set is changed:\n    - His month + 5 × 19 months, keeps the same month (though seasonal issues are more seasonally predictable).\n21. When the 21st set is changed:\n    - His month + 5 × 20 months (assuming the summer), which is a Summer issue, which was mentioned in step #6.\n22. When the 22nd set is changed:\n    - His month + 5 × 21 months (Summer again), which is a Summer issue, which was mentioned in step #17.\n23. When the 23rd set is changed:\n    - His month + 5 × 22 months (much later in Summer), which is a long Summer structure, which was mentioned in step #13.\n24. When the 25th set is changed:\n    - His month + 5 × 24 months (months into the next Summer), which is a longer structure than usual one, but it follows the summer structure, which was mentioned in step #3.\n25. When the 25th set is changed:\n    - His month + 4 + 12 = June, footnotes reveal how complicated it gets in actual seasons, as it happened in November going back to May (increase by 12 seasons, which is exactly half a year).\n\nPut into segments with repetition at 6 months:\n- Until spring: July 6-26\n- Second half yea