      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the month in which Hal will have to change the batteries for the 25th time, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the time intervals between changes:** We know that Hal changes the batteries every 5 months. This means that each new change occurs 4 months after the previous change (since 5 months + 1 month gap = 6 months).\n\n2. **Calculate the number of full 5-month periods between the 1st and 25th changes:** To do this, we divide 24 by 5 (because the first change is in May, which is the start point, so we need to count 24 full cycles of 5 months after the first change).\n   \\[\n   24 \\div 5 = 4.8\n   \\]\n   Since we need the next full 5-month period, we round up to the next whole number, which is 5. Therefore, the 25th change will occur exactly 5 full 5-month periods after the first change.\n\n3. **Determine the month for the 25th change:** If the first change is in May, we add 5 full 5-month periods to May.\n   - After 1 full 5-month period, it will be October (May + 4 months).\n   - After 2 full 5-month periods, it will be March (October + 4 months).\n   - After 3 full 5-month periods, it will be August (March + 4 months).\n   - After 4 full 5-month periods, it will be January (August + 4 months).\n   - After 5 full 5-month periods, it will be May (January + 4 months).\n\nTherefore, the 25th battery change will occur in \n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{May}}\n\\]",
