      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Hal changes the batteries every 5 months and he changed them in May the first time. To find out in which months Hal will change the batteries for the 25th time, we need to count 5 months from May 1. \n\n- May is the 5th month\n- The second change would be 5 + 5 = 10 months after May 1\n- The third change would be 10 + 5 = 15 months after May 1\n- The fourth change would be 15 + 5 = 20 months after May 1\n- The fifth change would be 20 + 5 = 25 months after May 1\n- The sixth change would be 25 + 5 = 30 months after May 1\n\nTherefore,\n- Jun is the 6th month\n- The seventh change will be 30 months plus 6 months which is 30 + 6 = 36 months after May 1\n- The eighth change would be 36 + 5 = 41 months after May 1\n- The ninth change would be 41 + 5 = 46 months after May 1\n- The tenth change would be 46 + 5 = 51 months after May 1\n\nWe can see that 51 is divisible by 12, implying Hal will achieve his 25th battery change on a day that falls within an eleventh or twelfth month.\n\nTo confirm:\n- The thirteenth change would be 51 + 12 = 63 months after May 1\n\nThis means that you will find your batteries changed for the 25th time in the eleventh month.\n\nHence our final answer is \n\\boxed{November}",
